+
+    DESKTOP WINDOW OPTIONS
+    ======================
+    On Windows, macOS and Linux, the nested struct sapp_desc.desktop creates
+    the window with options that are already in effect when the window
+    shows up for the first time, so that no decorated or activated window
+    flashes on screen:
+
+        .desktop.borderless     - the window has no title bar and no border
+        .desktop.topmost        - the window floats above normal windows
+        .desktop.no_focus       - the window never activates the application
+                                  and never takes the keyboard focus, not
+                                  even when it is clicked
+        .desktop.skip_taskbar   - the window has no taskbar button, and on
+                                  macOS the application has no Dock icon
+        .desktop.has_position   - the top left corner of the content area
+                                  opens at .desktop.x and .desktop.y instead
+                                  of the window being centered
+
+    The position has the same units as sapp_desc.width and sapp_desc.height,
+    with the origin at the top left corner of the primary screen and y
+    growing downward, on macOS too.
+
+    To let the window take the focus again, or to keep it from taking the
+    focus while the application runs, call:
 
+        sapp_set_window_focusable(bool focusable)
+
+    Together with SAPP_COMPOSITEMODE_PREMULTIPLIED, these options create
+    windows with per-pixel transparency that live directly on the desktop.
+    Transparency needs D3D11 on Windows, and a compositing window manager
+    with a 32-bit ARGB visual on Linux. When those are missing, sokol-app
+    fails with an error instead of creating an opaque window.
 
